                                "sense_id": "16aa869f-0447-373a-8bde-e853388b2065",
                                "text": "By the motion of the Heart, through the Emulgent Branches, the Blood is brought to the Kidneys, and is there freed of its Serum by their little Glands, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "68b0ca15-44ce-403c-aa0b-e3692e994fb4",
                                "sense_id": "16aa869f-0447-373a-8bde-e853388b2065",
                                "text": "...the kidneys, plac'd at the extremities of two large blood-vessels, the emulgent vein and artery, derived from the great vein and artery, very soon after their parting at the heart, the fountain of circulation."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
